WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.520
By the end of 6 Underground, almost all of
the characters have gone through complete

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.880
arcs, the themes have been clearly stated
and explored, and the pipe has been laid for

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.120
the inevitable sequel.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.200
You were probably just too busy watching things
blow up to notice.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.920
6 Underground foreshadows the ending to its
main plot fairly early.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.180
About half an hour into the movie, we see
a flashback in which One is in Paris, where

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.760
he meets the dictator of Turgistan, Rovach,
at a performance of Shakespeare's Richard

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.260
III.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.720
It's an important meeting.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.400
Rovach's smug attitude convinces One to found
his own paramilitary organization.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.180
Once its up and running, Rovach is its first
target.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.940
The play offers One and Rovach the opportunity
to trade barbs about how tyrants always get

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.410
their comeuppance, but the parallels between
Rovach's downfall and Richard III run deeper

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.060
than that.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.580
In the play, Richard keeps his brother Clarence
locked away in a tower, where he can't interfere

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:51.720
with Richard's plans.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.100
Rovach does the same thing to his brother
just swap the Tower of London for a Hong Kong

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:56.780
skyscraper.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:01.220
In addition, before Richard's downfall, he's
visited by an army of ghosts who predict his

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:01.720
demise.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.100
Naturally, it's One's group of "ghosts" who
invade Turgistan, turn the citizens against

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.440
Rovach, and break into the dictator's yacht,
leading to Rovach's death.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.060
Ultimately, it's not a bad thing.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:16.460
The closer the Ghosts get, the better they
work together, the more successful they become,

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.760
and the happier they are.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.040
By the end of the movie, they're a family
a dysfunctional one, sure, but a family just

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:22.540
the same.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.540
Despite what One says, he desperately wants
a family.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.280
You get a hint of that early on when you see
that the plane he crashes to fake his death

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.120
is full of pictures of his girlfriend.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.759
Even One's turn towards vigilantism is sparked
by family.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:40.030
He's inspired to found the Ghosts when delivering
medical supplies to Turgistan a stop that's

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.520
more about photo-ops than really helping people
and sees first-hand what happens when Rovach

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.400
uses chemical weapons on his own people.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:50.640
As One passes out gas masks, it's not the
mass suffering that makes One reconsider his

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:51.759
life choices.

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:54.829
It's the plight of a few children, separated
from their families.

00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:59.010
Ultimately, One accepts that personal connections
make you stronger, not weaker.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:01.950
After stopping Rovach's reign of terror, One
returns to New York.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:06.220
He clandestinely follows his ex, and realizes
that she has a four-year-old, blond-haired

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:06.980
child.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.819
We don't know for sure that the kid is One's,
but it seems pretty likely.

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:13.170
Before, One thought he had to give up his
life to help others.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:17.160
Now, he's has something to live for and he's
even more willing to fight for it.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.660
Almost every other Ghost goes through a similar
journey.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.820
When she was with the CIA, Two ignored her
emotions and followed orders she knew were

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:25.320
wrong.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.600
Three was disowned by his elderly mother for
his violent job, which ended up orphaning

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:30.610
a young girl.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.420
Four was abandoned by his friends after a
heist went sour.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.420
All of them decide to give up their normal
lives to join One, hoping to find redemption

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.240
along the way.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.680
Every one of these characters finds salvation
in their family.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.920
After Two and Three hook up in Las Vegas,
Two lets down her emotional barriers and pursues

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.060
a real relationship.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.560
Three introduces Two to his mom, and the son
and mother reconcile.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:55.420
After the Ghosts rescue Four from danger not
once but twice, the reformed thief realizes

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.519
he finally has friends he can trust.

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:01.410
6 Underground begins with a lot of talk about
the freedom death provides, but ends with

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.860
a monologue detailing how life gives us purpose.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.060
That's not an accident.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.260
Seven, played by Corey Hawkins, has a slightly
different arc.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.400
Seven already has people who love him.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:15.409
He doesn't join the team until after Six dies
during the Ghosts' first mission, leaving

00:03:15.409 --> 00:03:16.680
an opening in the squad.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:21.940
Before joining the Ghosts, Seven, or Blaine,
was an army sniper stationed in Afghanistan.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:26.909
One day, while surveilling a meeting, he spots
a terrorist masquerading as a U.N. representative.

00:03:26.909 --> 00:03:30.080
Blaine asks his superiors for permission to
shoot the man, but they decline.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.549
A bomb explodes, killing many of Blaine's
fellow soldiers.

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:37.409
Traumatized, Blaine returns home to find One
waiting for him with an offer: what if he

00:03:37.409 --> 00:03:41.160
could take down bad guys just like the ones
that killed his fellow soldiers?

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.520
"And I will never tell you not to pull that
trigger.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:48.800
What would you say to that?"

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.580
That's all that Blaine needs to sign up.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:56.640
Except it's not exactly true: The rest of
the Ghosts don't trust Seven, and One constantly

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.829
stops Blaine from following his instincts.

00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:03.140
When One tells Seven to abandon Four, who's
being chased by the bad guys, the former soldier

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:03.640
rebels.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.140
After Afghanistan, he won't lose another comrade.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.640
He pulls a gun on Three, who's driving, and
forces everyone to wait until Four.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.900
Later, Seven is the one who encourages everyone
to share their real names.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:18.280
During the film's climax, when One goes back
to save Four from certain death, we see how

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.740
much Four has rubbed off on him.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.600
Ultimately, Seven is the one who brings the
team together.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:25.850
He might've joined the Ghosts for different
reasons than everyone else, but they wouldn't

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:27.120
have become a family without him.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.110
By the end of 6 Underground, the Ghosts have
created a coup in Turgistan.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:35.670
Rovach is dead, and his pro-democracy brother
is in control.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.160
The civilians have been saved from another
round of chemical weapon attacks.

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.240
The squad is happy.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.260
The mission is done.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.820
But it's just the first mission.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.940
As One explains earlier in the movie, Rovach
was just the first name on the Ghosts' hit

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:47.440
list.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:48.520
There are eight more.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.440
Despite all of the setbacks, the Ghosts made
the world a slightly better place, but their

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.320
work isn't done.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.240
There are still bad people out there, and
the Ghosts are going to take 'em out.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:01.380
In other words: If 6 Underground is a hit,
Michael Bay and writers Rhett Reese and Paul

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.450
Wernick have already planted the seeds for
up to eight sequels.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.780
Hope you liked 6 Underground's unique concoction
of mayhem.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.700
You might be watching these movies forever.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.500
"Is this gonna work?

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:17.100
Well...I hope so, ha."

